          increasing data locality (coalescing), or by changing the cache configuration. Consider moving frequently     
          used data to shared memory. Stall samples are reported on the consumer instruction waiting for the result,    
          not necessarily on the producer. When this reason dominates, the kernel is memory-latency-bound, which is     
